uestion/worked-solution "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =6|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|+7|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =6(-2-0)-0+7(0-2) \\\\  & =6\\cdot (-2)+7\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-12-14 \\\\  & =-26\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-38176/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "979859e4-b60c-548d-8da6-b180400e1b07"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38176"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-38187/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "544eab82-41ec-557e-80f7-10720247f011" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38187/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "9a234bb1-11b9-5b3e-8ef5-8410508acc87" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38187/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "ae5bd86d-d5f8-5e04-87b9-25d303f20062" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38187/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "8a124bf0-1bdb-5e69-9294-36fdc430c8a0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38187/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "b0a9e27c-f893-5b0d-877f-04b4bd34735a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38187/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a8f03f3-eb38-540e-bdfe-b2d7ec4fcb96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-38187/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-38187/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-38187/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-38187/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-38187/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-38187/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-38187" :question/id #uuid "a5eb8a6b-37c6-54e6-b340-18101dbf3f8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-38187" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $N$ given below?\n\n- $N$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- $N$ is a singular matrix\n- $det(N)=-1$\n\n$$\nN=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7} & 3 & -\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ \\frac{1}{7} & 4 & -\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ \\frac{1}{7} & 5 & -\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(N) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7} & 3 & -\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ \\frac{1}{7} & 4 & -\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ \\frac{1}{7} & 5 & -\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}|\\begin{aligned}4 & -\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ 5 & -\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7} & -\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ \\frac{1}{7} & -\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}|+(-\\frac{1}{7})|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7} & 4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{7} & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}(-\\frac{4}{7}+\\frac{5}{7})-3(-\\frac{1}{49}+\\frac{1}{49})-\\frac{1}{7}(\\frac{5}{7}-\\frac{4}{7}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}-3\\cdot 0-\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{49}-\\frac{1}{49} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(N)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement II is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-38187/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38187"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-38179/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "f6e400dd-e15a-5c70-9ea8-d79b4678a3af" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38179/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "6c76a0cb-b92b-53a0-a6a6-ce3e8d11fbf0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38179/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "5987a13b-36d8-5878-86bb-d89d007e2f87" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38179/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "79c205fb-c281-5bc7-a08d-5148321446c5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38179/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "7f7be161-d6a6-5e3d-ae84-046cac1fe11e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38179/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "14fc5fd3-acb1-5e2d-848c-f71765f05031" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-38179/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-38179/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-38179/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-38179/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-38179/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-38179/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-38179" :question/id #uuid "08581ff2-f136-5cd3-82eb-06aac34673a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-38179" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $E$ given below?\n\n- $E$ is a singular matrix\n- $E$ is **not**  a singular matrix\n- $det(E)=-2$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 3 & 4 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 5 & 6 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 7 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(E) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 3 & 4 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 5 & 6 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 7 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 6 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 8\\end{aligned}|+4|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 5 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(40-42)-3(\\frac{16}{3}-\\frac{12}{3})+4(\\frac{14}{3}-\\frac{10}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}+4\\cdot \\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}-\\frac{12}{3}+\\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(E)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement I is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-38179/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38179"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-128500/selection/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" :answer/id #uuid "c4dbae3e-5235-57a9-9aa9-f81a548c19fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128500/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "f00d4c1f-15cf-5b01-be55-a79c1f05202c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128500/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "328ff454-e0e9-585e-a85a-9fa542f2a95d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128500/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "678d2bd2-d11f-5579-b305-c9942bcd3381" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128500/selection/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" :answer/id #uuid "ba948d9a-0adb-5139-b992-7e3ef6211177" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128500/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "04e27527-4ac1-5c1c-91d9-a7ed3ee291c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-128500/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-128500/selection/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" "q-128500/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-128500/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" "q-128500/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-128500/selection/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-128500" :question/id #uuid "6a11fa43-6c7e-5600-9b6b-53466b56fa48" :question/math-academy-id "q-128500" :question/problem "Given that\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ y & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nand $det(B)=12,$ find the value of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(B) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ y & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ y & 1\\end{aligned}|-5|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ y & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-2\\cdot (1-y)-5\\cdot (2-2y) \\\\  & =12y-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $12,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12y-12 & =12 \\\\ 12y & =24 \\\\ y & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-128500/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128500"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130580/selection/3871f2754fe42b0897438ca0ce1902bcd401d26cb163e43e529f232330ad0725" :answer/id #uuid "e4b8eb22-16db-5bab-8316-457b57a2c976" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5$ and $3$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130580/selection/99b2da47f0d1379c36e52e08f723d34a9f971bdb9a1e4d6f5fe1922a47d6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "ed49e64d-0484-58a6-8db9-8f727d6e97d4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$8$ and $3$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130580/selection/85ea3166d8581552c110ecfefd8eda3b60e95212192b46744bcc82bff8d53618" :answer/id #uuid "a1a82094-bf6c-5d9c-afc6-58825a1ac5dd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-8$ and $-1$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130580/selection/001cc7e8bf929756e2f4e5670d7d45b5b553506115e73023ed937544c5ac2883" :answer/id #uuid "53d6979c-b8d7-57d1-9f38-f4a05a09e7d3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-5$ and $-3$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130580/selection/b0e1e5c5fbfa9c8aa266dde747bdbbc3f38523038d811e4b47bb9b0a41916851" :answer/id #uuid "fa20b06c-807e-5188-a281-2600af857b24" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$7$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130580/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "726c649d-a64b-570b-a9ab-126c08e00ae0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130580/selection/85ea3166d8581552c110ecfefd8eda3b60e95212192b46744bcc82bff8d53618" :answer-field/choices ["q-130580/selection/3871f2754fe42b0897438ca0ce1902bcd401d26cb163e43e529f232330ad0725" "q-130580/selection/99b2da47f0d1379c36e52e08f723d34a9f971bdb9a1e4d6f5fe1922a47d6ffaa" "q-130580/selection/85ea3166d8581552c110ecfefd8eda3b60e95212192b46744bcc82bff8d53618" "q-130580/selection/001cc7e8bf929756e2f4e5670d7d45b5b553506115e73023ed937544c5ac2883" "q-130580/selection/b0e1e5c5fbfa9c8aa266dde747bdbbc3f38523038d811e4b47bb9b0a41916851"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130580" :question/id #uuid "dbd44e55-ce0f-5b5b-8e89-0724c2b1c4da" :question/math-academy-id "q-130580" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of\n$[\\begin{aligned}x & 2x & 3 \\\\ 5 & x & 7 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nis $22$, find all the possible values of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}x & 2x & 3 \\\\ 5 & x & 7 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =x|\\begin{aligned}x & 7 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2x|\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}5 & x \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =x(x-14)-2x(5-21)+3(10-3x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-14x+32x+30-9x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+9x+30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $22,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+9x+30 & =22 \\\\ {x}^{2}+9x+8 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{-9\\pm \\sqrt{{9}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 8}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-9\\pm \\sqrt{49}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-9\\pm 7}{2} \\\\  & =-8,-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-8$ and $x=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-130580/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130580"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-280540/field-1/0c1520f8fd536644d169b3ff4745bf8203dd48186469ce13c5ddf52a9dfc2d57" :answer/id #uuid "fbfce83b-d77a-539f-a673-3c1b57d43754" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280540/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b33d7a95-31e3-59e7-baff-78a70fb87d69" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280540/field-1/0c1520f8fd536644d169b3ff4745bf8203dd48186469ce13c5ddf52a9dfc2d57" :answer-field/choices ["q-280540/field-1/0c1520f8fd536644d169b3ff4745bf8203dd48186469ce13c5ddf52a9dfc2d57"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280540/field-2/6df66bf16371daf0619bc2276112595745e0ef481d5b99ebb766e9542fede5b8" :answer/id #uuid "a4fcc1b0-90f4-51c2-8119-f777b876fe0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280540/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed8b1ec8-ea6a-55e7-a205-8e82e5998c39" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280540/field-2/6df66bf16371daf0619bc2276112595745e0ef481d5b99ebb766e9542fede5b8" :answer-field/choices ["q-280540/field-2/6df66bf16371daf0619bc2276112595745e0ef481d5b99ebb766e9542fede5b8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280540" :question/id #uuid "91bf5b01-bba4-5542-be99-561e28debf43" :question/math-academy-id "q-280540" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of $[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ x & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ is $32$, find all the possible values of $x$ **in ascending order**.\n\nIn ascending order, $x=$\n{{field-1}} and $x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Let’s use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ x & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2)|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}x & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|+0 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2)(-2\\cdot 0-(-1)(4))-3(x\\cdot 0-(-1)(1)) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2)(4)-3(1) \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}-8-3 \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $32$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-11 & =32 \\\\ 4{x}^{2} & =43 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{43}{4} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{43}{4}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, **in ascending order**, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}$ and $x=\\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-280540/field-1" "q-280540/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-280540"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-14762"] :question/problem "Find the value of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/assets/8e7935fce161e2a1ed706ec03bb5cd202e8c4650ba01ca5e4633f9f1c121d04a.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-14763"] :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $A$ given below?\n\n- $\\det(A) = 0$\n\n- $A$ is **not** a singular matrix\n\n- $A$ is a singular matrix\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/assets/21cd71e00c682ad1117b9ae126adcbeb8e4c55769c73eae1e1169534f2a01d4a.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
